{"title":"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75a2d6d47afcf79e8493b06e33a20204d7102354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> be an infinite sequence of positive integers. Suppose that there is an integer<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e76751010708313d72288e79004a83967ed219da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> such that, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/9215186a5b621d0bda7948d36d29fb65b219f445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa014b9b7212304695bfcfd26018b6c6b08545b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_1}{a_2}+\\frac{a_2}{a_3}+\\dots +\\frac{a_{n-1}}{a_n}+\\frac{a_n}{a_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"216\" height=\"37\" /> is an integer. Prove that there is a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/7124ad318d97bd0e36bc33d4848ef015be90d4d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_m = a_{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748e82a1d40b6e04d4bd60081183993fdd31a278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\geq M.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The condition implies that the difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/f/f0f99ac1f76a8ec221964254b672e2bb8e0864be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) = \\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_1} - \\frac{a_n}{a_1} + \\frac{a_n}{a_{n+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"209\" height=\"38\" /> is an integer for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54df70ab4e8f05a9ad4b78a1dad57715beaca39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />. We proceed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-adic valuation only henceforth.\n</p><p><b><span style=\"color: red\">Claim:</span></b>   If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd1f60ef457e8929b6847f98a7436fc0b634df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\nmid a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/6945fe1c64532cdaa1129c7b7d271c8864a89d76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_{n+1}) \\le \\nu_p(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee0cd3e9251aacd34807aac66469a427866e4e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  \tThe first two terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> have nonnegative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb182a99f817f3d85ce03b80f4758c118711e20f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, \tso we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e05adbb400960a005fb3fceb70a777a8d4c50c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(\\frac{a_n}{a_{n+1}}) \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><b><span style=\"color: red\">Claim:</span></b>  \tIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/2/9325539a5b931ac1afe2c17d9a9308f68d44fc0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/60172840072a3f50f9fe52bc2891d316c47fd691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> is eventually constant.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  \tBy hypothesis <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea46ee7269d89f02f3162574bf7c85b9fc19860.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_1) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />. \tWe consider two cases. \n</p>\n<ol>\n<li>First assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/9539b576b6ae5ec00833bbbea2420cae2ed1ba86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_k) \\ge \\nu_p(a_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038008fb83bbb21fdb2aa33a19e967f9c18543c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />. \t\tWe claim that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd614aab3401d541b41d996669ed8ab088c7fc77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> we have: \t\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/86671bb6bf6e7dcf144830571a18cc79cb7d42d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\nu_p(a_1) \\le \\nu_p(a_{n+1}) \\le \\nu_p(a_n).\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"19\" /> \t\tThis is just by induction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />; \t\tfrom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62ea3e316d10a7cf6cd6215c52b9d81e449dd22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu(\\frac{a_n}{a_1}) \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" />, we have \t\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/3/4c3ba7d46e1384ce151290ad1600ff62f483364c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\nu_p\\left( \\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_1} + \\frac{a_n}{a_{n+1}} \\right) \\ge 0\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"43\" /> \t\twhich implies the displayed inequality \t\t(since otherwise exactly one term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> has nonnegative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb182a99f817f3d85ce03b80f4758c118711e20f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />). \t\tThus once we reach this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/60172840072a3f50f9fe52bc2891d316c47fd691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> is monotic but bounded below by \t\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08e4dfadd54b49ebdb8fcdc96574aec3c4b0e8b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" />, and so it is eventually constant.</li>\n\n<li>Now assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820ecb17d6b29311c9db8199bc2f4d5fea766d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_k) &lt; \\nu_p(a_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038008fb83bbb21fdb2aa33a19e967f9c18543c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />. \t\tTake any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a54df70ab4e8f05a9ad4b78a1dad57715beaca39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> then. \t\tWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f186145c66e973642b485effc5512550fd91cbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p\\left(\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_1}\\right) &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"120\" height=\"45\" />, \t\tand also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad00f15dadf5d796d30b8f0e5be860a9bb838cb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p\\left(\\frac{a_n}{a_1}\\right) &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"104\" height=\"45\" />, \t\tso among the three terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />, \t\ttwo must have equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-adic valuation. \t\tWe consider all three possibilities: \t\t\\begin{align*} \t\t\t\\nu_p\\left(\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_1}\\right) = \\nu_p\\left(\\frac{a_n}{a_1}\\right) \t\t\t&amp;\\implies \\boxed{\\nu_p(a_{n+1}) = \\nu_p(a_{n})} \\\\ \t\t\t\\nu_p\\left(\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_1}\\right) = \\nu_p\\left(\\frac{a_n}{a_{n+1}}\\right) \t\t\t&amp;\\implies \\boxed{\\nu_p(a_{n+1}) = \\frac{\\nu_p(a_n) + \\nu_p(a_1)}{2}} \\\\ \t\t\t\\nu_p\\left(\\frac{a_{n}}{a_1}\\right) = \\nu_p\\left(\\frac{a_n}{a_{n+1}}\\right) \t\t\t&amp;\\implies \\nu_p(a_{n+1}) = \\nu_p(a_1),\\text{ but this is impossible}. \t\t\\end{align*} \t\tThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/734d6087c9a5de83ae5536ae98396974be80aef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_{n+1}) \\ge \\nu_p(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" /> \t\tand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/60172840072a3f50f9fe52bc2891d316c47fd691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> is bounded above by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08e4dfadd54b49ebdb8fcdc96574aec3c4b0e8b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" />. \t\tSo in this case we must also stabilize.<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /></li>\n</ol>\n<p>Since the latter claim is applied only to finitely many primes, after some time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/60172840072a3f50f9fe52bc2891d316c47fd691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> is fixed for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/2/9325539a5b931ac1afe2c17d9a9308f68d44fc0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />. Afterwards, the sequence satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a0ee9e611cddf508f73c706b41cc1edff069e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} \\mid a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and thus must be eventually constant.\n</p><p><b><span style=\"color: red\">Remark:</span></b>  \tThis solution is almost completely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-adic, \tin the sense that I think a similar result if one replaces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ef623097625e4af0629b338b38b3d606b6a112.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n \\in {\\mathbb Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> \tby <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/4582efb2c661e01a96a89ae0d38e11ca5d663f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n \\in {\\mathbb Z}_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" /> for any particular prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. \tIn other words, the primes almost do not talk to each other.\n</p><p>There is one caveat: if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer sequence \tsuch that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d42da2a3331688cedf0aa0539788ca0747336b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" /> is eventually constant for each prime \tthen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> may not be constant. \tFor example, take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> to be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th prime! \tThat's why in the first claim (applied to co-finitely many of the primes), \twe need the stronger non-decreasing condition, \trather than just eventually constant.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO\" title=\"2018 IMO\">2018 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018005402\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 313/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10163/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.775      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.775      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16487:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018005402 and revision id 271723. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}